# Users — /api/users
#
# Run `dotnet run --project JsonApiPoc` first, then click the gutter icon next to a request.
# `###` separates requests; the text after it is the request name. "->" notes the expected outcome.
#
# Users are the CRM's sales reps — they own deals. Seed: 1 Sarah Chen, 2 Marcus Webb.
# Read-only, and the simplest map in the API: two attributes, no relationships.

@host = http://localhost:5031

### List users (deal owners)
GET {{host}}/api/users
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Sorted by name
GET {{host}}/api/users?sort=name
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Sorted by email, descending
GET {{host}}/api/users?sort=-email
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### One per page -> links.next, meta.pageCount
GET {{host}}/api/users?page[size]=1
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Sparse fieldset: names only
GET {{host}}/api/users?fields[users]=name
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Single user
GET {{host}}/api/users/1
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Missing user -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/users/999
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

# Reached the other way round, from a deal that owns it:
#   GET /api/deals/1/owner              (the full user)
#   GET /api/deals/1/relationships/owner (just the identifier)
# Both live in Deals.http.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Query validation -> 400 problem details
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Unsupported sort field -> 400 (detail lists name, email)
GET {{host}}/api/users?sort=height
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Users expose no includes -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/users?include=deals
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Unknown query parameter -> 400 (strict validation)
GET {{host}}/api/users?foo=bar
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Paging a single-resource endpoint -> 400 (only collections paginate)
GET {{host}}/api/users/1?page[number]=2
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
